---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Technical Watchlist & Deep Dives | Mohammad Yahia" description="Curated reading track, research books, and courses across distributed systems, security, and architecture.">
  <section class="section-heading" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <span class="eyebrow">Continuous Learning</span>
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.8rem);">
      Technical Deep-Dive Dashboard
    </h1>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 50rem;">
      A curated track of ongoing learning, research books, and architecture courses across distributed systems, enterprise security, and software design.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="watch-grid">
    <!-- COLUMN 1: Currently Analyzing -->
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0;">Currently Analyzing</h2>
      </div>

      <article class="watch-card">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
          <span class="watch-type-tag">Book</span>
          <span class="meta" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">Martin Kleppmann</span>
        </div>

        <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem;">
          Designing Data-Intensive Applications
        </h3>
        
        <p class="meta" style="font-size: 0.88rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          The Big Ideas Behind Reliable, Scalable, and Maintainable Systems
        </p>

        <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
          Deep-diving into database engine internals, LSM-trees vs B-Trees, partitioning mechanics, distributed replication, consensus protocols (Raft/Paxos), and stream processing primitives.
        </p>

        <div class="article-tags">
          <span class="tag-chip">Distributed Systems</span>
          <span class="tag-chip">Storage Engines</span>
          <span class="tag-chip">Stream Processing</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="watch-card">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
          <span class="watch-type-tag">Course</span>
          <span class="meta" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">Aaron Parecki</span>
        </div>

        <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem;">
          The Nuts and Bolts of OAuth 2.0
        </h3>
        
        <p class="meta" style="font-size: 0.88rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Enterprise Authorization & Identity Flows
        </p>

        <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
          Mastering secure enterprise authorization loops, PKCE flows, JWT verification, scope hierarchies, security architecture validation, and zero-trust API protection.
        </p>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/oauth-2-simplified/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="section-link" style="font-size: 0.85rem;">
            Course Link ↗
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="article-tags">
          <span class="tag-chip">OAuth 2.0</span>
          <span class="tag-chip">OIDC</span>
          <span class="tag-chip">Zero-Trust</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- COLUMN 2: Up Next in the Queue -->
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;">
        <span style="width: 0.55rem; height: 0.55rem; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--muted);"></span>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0;">Up Next in Queue</h2>
      </div>

      <article class="watch-card">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
          <span class="watch-type-tag">Course</span>
          <span class="meta" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">Enterprise Masterclass</span>
        </div>

        <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem;">
          Software Architecture Essentials: Masterclass
        </h3>
        
        <p class="meta" style="font-size: 0.88rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Advanced System Patterns & Isolation Strategies
        </p>

        <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
          Analyzing component isolation strategies, resilience engineering (circuit breakers, bulkheads), event sourcing, CQRS patterns, and systematic scalability trade-offs.
        </p>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/software-architecture-essentials/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="section-link" style="font-size: 0.85rem;">
            Course Link ↗
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="article-tags">
          <span class="tag-chip">System Design</span>
          <span class="tag-chip">Enterprise Architecture</span>
          <span class="tag-chip">Scalability</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

